# One-way valve, layer 1: default deny (DR-002; reversed after adversarial verification on 2026-08-24)
#
# The first design ignored only `state/` and `_private/` and tracked everything else. Verification showed why
# that was wrong: README and SETUP tell users to keep documents, notes, and tracks in this workspace, so ordinary
# paths such as `company/tracker.md` could commit company data. A denylist blocks only paths already imagined.
#
# The design was reversed: ignore everything, then restore only the engine. New files stay outside Git by
# default; engine changes are tracked deliberately. Mistakes now fail in the safer direction.
#
# Conversely, this repository does not back up instance data. Arrange that backup separately (CHECKLIST.md).
#
# To add an engine file, add one line to the allowlist below. That line is the decision point.

# Deny everything.
/*

# Restore only the engine.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/README.ko.md
!/LICENSE
!/SETUP.md
!/SETUP.ko.md
!/CHECKLIST.md
!/CHECKLIST.ko.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CHANGELOG.ko.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/AGENTS.ko.md
!/setup.sh
!/tools/
!/templates/
!/system/
!/.claude/
!/.codex/
!/state/
!/.github/

# Deny these paths again inside restored directories.
# Instance configuration. Its template is tracked under templates/.
/system/memory-config.json
/system/memory-config.json.*
/system/instance-rules.md
# Instance-owned rules pair with upstream files (KIT-DR-004).
/system/rituals.local.md
/system/decisions.md
# Generated files.
/system/memory-map.html
/system/build-log.md
# Cross-runtime debate: track only the README rules; prompts, logs, and rounds belong to the instance.
/system/debate/*
!/system/debate/README.md
!/system/debate/README.ko.md
# All state belongs to the instance. Keep only the directory placeholder.
/state/*
!/state/.gitkeep
# Claude local settings, including permission allowlists, belong to the machine.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Miscellaneous.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
